            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:PathIntegralForAbelianChernSimonsWilsonLoops"} (9)
            satisfies enough structural properties that are
            %em suggested
            by the symbols on the right as to be uniquely fixed by these conditions — and then take that to be the definition.
          %p
            We proceed
            %a{:href => "#AbelianCSWilsonLoopsViaGaussianIntegrals"} below
            to discuss the usual such postulates, which proceed by applying expected properties of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gaussian+integrals"} Gaussian integrals
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#GuadagniniThuillier08"} Guadagnini &amp; Thuillier 2008 §4.3
          %h4#AbelianCSWilsonLoopsViaGaussianIntegrals The Gaussian path integral
          %p
            Since the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+Chern-Simons+theory"} abelian Chern-Simons
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+density"} Lagrangian density
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
