            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Hahn04b"} 2004b
          %p
            But
            %a{:href => "#Witten89"} Witten 1989 p. 363
            asserted that it is “clear” that the following “point-splitting regularization” should be used instead, and this has become the commonly accepted choice since (cf.
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Kaul99"} Kaul 1999 (9)
