          .footnotes
            %hr/
            %ol
              %li#fn:1
                %p
                  Beware that
                  %a{:href => "#Witten89"} Witten 1989
                  drops a factor of 2 in passing from (1.3) to (2.27) there. This amounts to shifting the Chern-Simons level “
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                  ” — our
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi K
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
                  %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:TheLagrangianDensity"} (2)
                  — by a factor of 2. His end result for the Wilson loop, equation (2.31) there, is expressed with respect to this shifted level. Transforming back to the original and usual normalization in (1.3) there cancels the factor of 2 in (2.31) there, which thereby agrees with our
                  %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:AbelianCSWilsonLoopsInTermsOfFramingAndLinkingNumbers"} (14)
                  (under
                  = succeed ")." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi k
                            %mi there
                          %mo =
                          %msub
                            %mi K
                            %mi here
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k_{there} = K_{here}
                  %a{:href => "#Kaul99"} Kaul 1999
                  follows along with a lost factor of 2 in (1) there and hence gives in (9) there Witten’s formula, while
                  %a{:href => "#MezeiPufuWang17"} Mezei, Pufu &amp; Wang 2017 (5.1)
                  appear to have noticed the glitch. Unfortunately, this is all the more confusing as there is generally an ambiguity of a factor of 2 in what one may want to mean by the abelian Chern-Simons level in the first place, as discussed
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a{:href => "#LagrangianDensityAndLevel"} above
                  %a{:href => "#fnref:1", :rev => "footnote"} ↩
